## 12. COPY, EDIT, AND REGENERATION BEHAVIOR

### Copy

Every result card has a working Copy button.

Use the Clipboard API where available, with an appropriate fallback when supported.

Show clear feedback such as "COPIED!" when copying succeeds.

If clipboard access fails, explain how the user can copy the selected text manually.

### Edit

Make each generated output editable.

The user must be able to modify a result before copying it.

Editing one card must not alter any other result.

### Regenerate one mode

Regenerate only the selected mode.

Send the original input, the selected mode instructions, and any relevant prior result context to Gemini.

Preserve the other three results and any edits the user has made to them.

Ask for a fresh, meaning-preserving variation rather than a near-duplicate.

If the selected result has been edited manually, avoid overwriting it without confirmation.

### Regenerate all

Generate a fresh set of four transformations.

If existing results have manual edits, confirm before replacing them.

### Copy all

Copy a clearly labeled version of the four current results, preserving the user's edits.

Use a format such as:

NATURAL AMERICAN
[Text]

CASUAL & SLANG
[Text]

UNFILTERED & BLUNT
[Text]

BADASS & CONFIDENT
[Text]

Do not include educational explanations unless the user explicitly selects an option to include them.

